1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,333
Most smart bathrooms fail for one simple reason: sensors hate steam.

2
00:00:07,333 --> 00:00:17,333
PIR motion sensors cannot see through glass shower cabins, mmWave radars suffer from reflection noise, and battery sensors die in high humidity.

3
00:00:17,333 --> 00:00:25,500
Even worse, naive rules like "turn light on when door closes" leave you stepping into pitch darkness.

4
00:00:25,533 --> 00:00:34,000
Instead of struggling with wireless sensors inside the shower, Apartment Thread exploits the bathroom door as an absolute physical boundary.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:42,667
We use a ₹57 MC-38 wired magnetic reed switch mounted on the exterior door jamb—completely isolated from interior moisture.

6
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:54,433
When the gap is under 15mm, the dry contact closes with zero battery maintenance and perpetual reliability.

7
00:00:54,467 --> 00:01:03,000
In typical Indian apartments, a modular switchboard sits right next to the bathroom door frame.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:11,667
We pull a 2-core wire through concealed conduit directly into input S2 of a Tinxy smart switch, leaving Relay 2 unconnected as a dummy channel.

9
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:20,333
Input S2 triggers a hardware GPIO interrupt in under 5ms on the ESP8266 silicon with zero wireless latency.

10
00:01:20,367 --> 00:01:28,667
State 1: Opening the door immediately turns the light ON (<5ms)—illuminating the threshold before you enter.

11
00:01:28,667 --> 00:01:37,333
State 2: Closing the door locks the vanity light and exhaust fan ON indefinitely—completely immune to shower steam or stillness.

12
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:46,000
State 3: Opening the door to exit starts a gentle 60-second vacancy countdown and ventilation dissipation cycle.

13
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:56,100
State 4: When the timer expires, the lights shut off automatically. A self-correcting loop that never desyncs.

14
00:01:56,133 --> 00:02:04,667
The entire pattern is 100% local-first. If Wi-Fi drops or Home Assistant crashes, the switchboard operates identically on local silicon.

15
00:02:04,667 --> 00:02:13,667
Standard physical rocker switches preserve manual override at all times, backed by a 45-minute safety watchdog.

16
00:02:13,667 --> 00:02:22,767
High-reliability residential automation retrofitted into standard Indian modular switchboards for under ₹1,500 INR.
